    "Sixteen whole source bodies preserve the unmasked gray/ivory ridged head, four mandibles/one gold ring, gray-black gold-banded tendrils, netting and own trophy straps, RIGHT paired blades, LEFT caster/computer and small partly visible antique pistol at LEFT waist. Pistol model/hidden parts and tiny glyphs remain unresolved.",
    "S08 actually raises LEFT knee despite requested RIGHT; gesture/torso differ from S06. Requested and observed text are retained; no flip or limb replacement corrects it in software.",
    "Whole connected pose extraction/nearest satellite assignment with bounded4px weak-alpha fringe, translations and one common nearest scale only. All alpha>12 source pixels assigned before scaling; no mirrored, repainted, recolored, duplicated or synthesized pose.",
    "The shared foot baseline is a packing measurement, not a claim all feet are grounded: raised walk/recoil feet were inspected whole. Source JPEG embedded AdobeRGB is handled by Sharp ICC-aware sRGB decode for technical PNG conversion; RGB equality is scoped to that decoder.",
    "Only the dated new PNG/audit are installed; root alone updates runtime selection and retains the old atlas as an accessible variant."
